From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: hold 5 s after the SCM result print in kreset (panel capture window)

REVIEW-20261031-1930 F-1: the SCM download-mode result line
prints microseconds before PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, so no panel
capture can ever read it - and a boot cycle PASS cannot
distinguish a clean TTL reset from an early crash that also
returns to pmOS. kreset now busy-waits ~5 s on the generic
counter (cntvct_el0 / cntfrq_el0, the same registers StallWatch
polls) between the result print and the reset, so the R-3
webcam burst has a window that contains the line.

Gated on the same qcom-dload-mode-clear feature as the print:
builds without the feature are untouched. Deliberately NOT in
emergency_reset: that path must reset immediately. A zero
counter frequency degenerates to no hold.

---
diff --git a/src/arch/aarch64/stop.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/stop.rs
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/stop.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/stop.rs
@@ -10,12 +10,30 @@ fn halt_after_failed_psci(operation: &str, error: psci::CallError) -> ! {
     }
 }
 
+/// Hold the framebuffer console for ~5 s after the SCM download-mode
+/// result is printed, so a panel capture can actually read the line
+/// before the reset fires (REVIEW-20261031-1930 F-1). Timer-based busy
+/// wait on the generic counter, the same registers StallWatch polls;
+/// a zero counter frequency degenerates to no hold.
+#[cfg(feature = "qcom-dload-mode-clear")]
+fn panel_capture_hold() {
+    use crate::arch::device::cpu::registers::control_regs;
+    println!("kreset: holding 5 s before SYSTEM_RESET (panel capture window)");
+    let started = unsafe { control_regs::cntvct_el0() };
+    let limit = u64::from(unsafe { control_regs::cntfrq_el0() }).saturating_mul(5);
+    while unsafe { control_regs::cntvct_el0() }.wrapping_sub(started) < limit {
+        core::hint::spin_loop();
+    }
+}
+
 pub unsafe fn kreset() -> ! {
     #[cfg(feature = "qcom-dload-mode-clear")]
     match crate::arch::device::qcom_scm::clear_download_mode() {
         Ok(()) => { info!("qcom SCM: download-mode cleared"); }
         Err(reason) => { warn!("Qualcomm SCM download-mode clear failed: {}", reason); }
     }
+    #[cfg(feature = "qcom-dload-mode-clear")]
+    panel_capture_hold();
     println!("kreset: PSCI SYSTEM_RESET (0x84000009)");
     match psci::system_reset() {
         Ok(()) => unreachable!(),
